english_question:
In the figure, the edge length of the cube ABCD-A₁B₁C₁D₁ is 1, and E is the midpoint of A₁B₁. Given the following four statements: 
① The distance from point E to the plane ABC₁D₁ is $ \frac {1}{2}$; 
② The angle between line BC and plane ABC₁D₁ is 45°; 
③ The minimum projection area of the spatial quadrilateral ABCD₁ within the six faces of the cube is $ \frac {1}{2}$; 
④ Among all the edges of the cube, there are 5 edges that are coplanar with AB and CC₁. 
How many of the above statements are correct?

In the 4\( \times \)4 square shown in the image, the numbers 1, 2, 3, …, 16 are written. The square is folded in the following four steps: 
 (1) The upper half is folded over the lower half; 
 (2) The lower half is folded over the upper half; 
 (3) The right half is folded over the left half; 
 (4) The left half is folded over the right half. What is the top number after these four folds?

